{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-04T09:32:51.686Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"259b6fa8d51ec5e6f7d340fb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-vcs-v5bg"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Stop concurrent test packs from rewriting the shared build"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"installPackedExtension ran npm pack --silent in the package root. npm pack runs prepack (npm run build = tsc), which truncates and rewrites dist/. The release suite runs up to 4 test files concurrently, so one file's tsc rewrote dist/ while another file's npm pack archived it, and node-tar failed with EOF 'encountered unexpected EOF' on a dist file. --silent suppressed that npm error, so the test diagnostic showed only the prepare script's benign 'npm pack: skipping merge-driver install during artifact creation' line. Seen on main 131dc3a (test (22): bisect.test.ts walk-killed test) and on #177 (test (26): checkpoints.test.ts installed-CLI test). Reproduced locally: 3/60 and 5/60 staggered concurrent packs failed with EOF on dist files."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","concurrency","flaky-test","testing"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-04T09:32:51.686Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-04T09:32:51.686Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude-hub"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"installPackedExtension packs the existing build with --ignore-scripts (as composition-consumer.test.ts and verify-pack-privacy.ts already do) and --loglevel=error so npm's own error reaches the diagnostic; a regression test proves a real pack leaves every dist/ file mtime unchanged and fails when the old --silent arguments are restored; 60 staggered concurrent packs with the new arguments all succeed with empty stderr."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Concurrent test files pack the extension without corrupting each other's archive."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"scripts/pm-environment"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"c3b27f9042d3523738f549f0945d1e9550ec98a6f43ce4b2cc632cb8e6cd8569","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"01a5645a7a24f4bddc1d26416fa541ad3375a7547071810f56841c931aa94ad7"}
